---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The VOLI App: Fantasy, Live Volleyball, Stats & History"
  description="Fantasy volleyball, live college and pro volleyball, box scores, play-by-play, the VOLI Top 100, the Volleyball Encyclopedia, news and podcasts. Free."
  ogUrl="https://playvoli.com/mobileapp"
>
    <main class="card">
        <img src="/images/appicon_sm.webp" alt="VOLI" class="app-icon">
        <h1 class="title">The VOLI App</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">Free on iPhone and Android. Launched January 2026.</p>

        <div class="store-buttons">
            <div class="store-col">
                <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/voli-the-volleyball-hub/id6749812982" class="btn-store" target="_blank">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="white" width="28" height="28">
                        <path d="M17.05 20.28c-.98.95-2.05.8-3.08.35-1.09-.46-2.09-.48-3.24 0-1.44.62-2.2.44-3.06-.35C2.79 15.25 3.51 7.59 9.05 7.31c1.35.07 2.29.74 3.08.8 1.18-.24 2.31-.93 3.57-.84 1.51.12 2.65.72 3.4 1.8-3.12 1.87-2.38 5.98.48 7.13-.57 1.5-1.31 2.99-2.54 4.09l.01-.01zM12.03 7.25c-.15-2.23 1.66-4.07 3.74-4.25.29 2.58-2.34 4.5-3.74 4.25z"/>
                    </svg>
                    <div class="btn-store-text">
                        <span class="btn-store-label">Download on the</span>
                        <span class="btn-store-name">App Store</span>
                    </div>
                </a>
                <div class="rating-stars">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="#F0FF1E"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg>
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="#F0FF1E"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg>
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="#F0FF1E"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg>
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="#F0FF1E"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg>
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="#F0FF1E"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="store-downloads">
                <span class="store-downloads-num">2.6k+</span>
                <span class="store-downloads-label">downloads</span>
            </div>
            <div class="store-col">
                <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.playvoli.app" class="btn-store" target="_blank">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="white" width="28" height="28">
                        <path d="M3.609 1.814L13.792 12 3.61 22.186a.996.996 0 01-.61-.92V2.734a1 1 0 01.609-.92zm10.89 10.893l2.302 2.302-10.937 6.333 8.635-8.635zm3.199-3.198l2.807 1.626a1 1 0 010 1.73l-2.808 1.626L15.206 12l2.492-2.491zM5.864 2.658L16.802 8.99l-2.303 2.303-8.635-8.635z"/>
                    </svg>
                    <div class="btn-store-text">
                        <span class="btn-store-label">Get it on</span>
                        <span class="btn-store-name">Google Play</span>
                    </div>
                </a>
                <div class="rating-stars">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="#F0FF1E"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg>
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="#F0FF1E"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg>
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="#F0FF1E"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg>
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="#F0FF1E"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg>
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="#F0FF1E"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-label">The App</div>
            <p class="section-text">VOLI is one free app for NCAA Division I women's volleyball, Major League Volleyball (MLV) and LOVB. Play fantasy with your friends, follow matches live, look up any player or team, see where teams rank, and go back through the sport's history to 1979, with news, podcasts and chat alongside. Figures below are as of September 2026.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-label">What's Inside</div>

            <nav class="tabs" aria-label="App sections">
                <a class="tab" href="#fantasy"><img src="/images/icons/fantasy_opt.png" alt="" class="tab-icon"><span>Fantasy</span></a>
                <a class="tab" href="#live-games"><img src="/images/icons/games_opt.png" alt="" class="tab-icon"><span>Live Games</span></a>
                <a class="tab" href="#stats"><img src="/images/icons/statistics_opt.png" alt="" class="tab-icon"><span>Stats</span></a>
                <a class="tab" href="#rankings"><span>Rankings</span></a>
                <a class="tab" href="#encyclopedia"><span>Encyclopedia</span></a>
                <a class="tab" href="#content"><img src="/images/icons/content_opt.png" alt="" class="tab-icon"><span>News &amp; Podcasts</span></a>
                <a class="tab" href="#community"><img src="/images/icons/community_opt.png" alt="" class="tab-icon"><span>Community</span></a>
            </nav>

            <div class="panels">
            <section class="panel" id="fantasy">
                <h2 class="panel-title">Fantasy Volleyball</h2>
                <p class="panel-lede">Contract-based fantasy leagues for NCAA Division I women's volleyball and Major League Volleyball. Build a roster of real players under a salary cap, sign them to multi-round contracts, and score points from their real match stats. Play in a private league with friends or join a public league run by a volleyball podcast.</p>
                <p class="panel-note">The NCAA season runs in ten rounds, each Wednesday through Sunday, with Monday and Tuesday as the signing window. Trades, bench swaps, a global leaderboard and a guided setup are built in.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="panel" id="live-games">
                <h2 class="panel-title">Live Scores &amp; Play-by-Play</h2>
                <p class="panel-lede">Live scores, schedules, box scores, set-by-set scoring and play-by-play for college and pro matches: more than <strong>18,000 matches</strong> played since 2023. Play-by-play covers all <strong>445 MLV and LOVB matches</strong> since 2024 and more than <strong>360,000 NCAA rallies</strong> in the 2026 season, with substitutions, starting lineups, the rotation on court and a lead chart for each set.</p>
                <p class="panel-note">On iPhone, Live Activities keep the score on your lock screen, and a home-screen widget shows your next game. Calendar sync and where-to-watch links are built in. <a href="/game-center">Follow a match live →</a></p>
            </section>

            <section class="panel" id="stats">
                <h2 class="panel-title">Volleyball Statistics</h2>
                <p class="panel-lede">Nearly <strong>480,000 NCAA player box-score lines</strong> since 2023, covering 99.8% of completed Division I matches: kills, attack errors, hitting percentage, aces, receptions, assists, blocks and digs. Pro matches carry set-by-set player stats and graded skill stats for attack, serve, receive, block, dig and set.</p>
                <p class="panel-note">Leaderboards sort by season, position, conference, class and round. Player and team pages carry game logs, history and rosters. <a href="/ncaa-volleyball">College volleyball →</a> · <a href="/pro-volleyball">Pro volleyball →</a></p>
            </section>

            <section class="panel" id="rankings">
                <h2 class="panel-title">Rankings &amp; Win Probabilities</h2>
                <p class="panel-lede">The <strong>VOLI Top 100</strong> ranks Division I teams from match results and strength of schedule, published each Monday. Before first serve, each upcoming college match shows each team's chance to win and the most likely set score, from 3-0 to 0-3.</p>
                <p class="panel-note"><a href="/rankings">The VOLI Top 100 →</a> · <a href="/methods">How VOLI's numbers work →</a></p>
            </section>

            <section class="panel" id="encyclopedia">
                <h2 class="panel-title">The Volleyball Encyclopedia</h2>
                <p class="panel-lede">More than <strong>18,000 honors back to 1979</strong>: 3,000+ AVCA All-America selections since 1981, AVCA Players and Coaches of the Year, All-Region teams, ACC, Big 12, Big Ten and SEC honors, and MLV, LOVB and Athletes Unlimited awards. Also the AVCA Coaches Poll archive since 1982, all 45 NCAA champions, NCAA and pro record books, and the MLV Draft.</p>
                <p class="panel-note"><a href="/encyclopedia">Explore the Encyclopedia →</a></p>
            </section>

            <section class="panel" id="content">
                <h2 class="panel-title">Volleyball News &amp; Podcasts</h2>
                <p class="panel-lede">
                    Read volleyball news and listen to volleyball podcasts in one place.
                    VOLI gathers coverage from <strong>19 outlets</strong> &mdash; league and conference sites and
                    independent writers &mdash; and links every story to its source. It carries <strong>13 volleyball podcasts</strong> with nearly
                    <strong>900 episodes</strong> (about 750 hours), streamable and downloadable inside the app.
                </p>
                <p class="panel-note">Coverage spans NCAA women's volleyball, Major League Volleyball, LOVB, team announcements, transfers, rankings and award news. Articles are read in-app with comments, reactions and player and team tagging.</p>

                <h3 class="panel-sub">Volleyball podcasts on VOLI</h3>
                <ul class="pod-grid">
                    <li><span class="pod-name">Volley Talk with Sarah Pavan</span><span class="pod-meta">Sarah Pavan &middot; 93 episodes</span><span class="pod-tag">Partner</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">The Major League Minute</span><span class="pod-meta">MLM &middot; 48 episodes</span><span class="pod-tag">Partner</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">Court Captains</span><span class="pod-meta">KWND Studios &middot; 67 episodes</span><span class="pod-tag">Partner</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">The USA Volleyball Show</span><span class="pod-meta">USA Volleyball &middot; 152 episodes</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">Volleyball State</span><span class="pod-meta">Jeff Sheldon &amp; Lincoln Arneal &middot; 133 episodes</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">Dig City</span><span class="pod-meta">Purdue Volleyball &middot; 127 episodes</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">The Side Out Society Podcast</span><span class="pod-meta">Side Out Society &middot; 60 episodes</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">Serving Pancakes</span><span class="pod-meta">iHeartPodcasts &middot; 60 episodes</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">Ember's Nest</span><span class="pod-meta">Edward White &middot; 48 episodes</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">Set 6: The Official MLV Podcast</span><span class="pod-meta">Major League Volleyball &middot; 23 episodes</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">Six Zone Duo</span><span class="pod-meta">Amie Just &amp; Erin Sorensen &middot; 6 episodes</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">Volley Takes</span><span class="pod-meta">Abby Benton &middot; 33 episodes</span></li>
                    <li><span class="pod-name">Out of Rotation</span><span class="pod-meta">Dan Meske &middot; 34 episodes</span></li>
                </ul>
                <p class="panel-note">Every episode streams or downloads for offline listening, with playback position synced across devices. Partner podcasts run their own fantasy leagues, AMAs and Take of the Talk sessions inside VOLI. <a href="/news-and-podcasts">Read and listen →</a></p>
            </section>

            <section class="panel" id="community">
                <h2 class="panel-title">Volleyball Community</h2>
                <p class="panel-lede">Chat rooms for each match, team and league, AMAs with volleyball creators, the weekly Creators Poll, conference pick'em, and the Daily Grid, a new volleyball trivia grid each day.</p>
                <p class="panel-note"><a href="/dailygrid">Play the Daily Grid →</a></p>
            </section>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-label">Voli User Testimonials</div>
            <div class="testimonials">
                <div class="testimonial">
                    <p>"This app is everything I've been dreaming of since I've gotten into professional volleyball!"</p>
                </div>
                <div class="testimonial">
                    <p>"It was already so fun to watch volleyball before but now it's a completely new experience watching for your fantasy league. LOVE IT!"</p>
                </div>
                <div class="testimonial">
                    <p>"I've spent years watching my brothers play fantasy football and basketball while wondering 'when can I do this for my sport?' So thank you!!"</p>
                </div>
                <div class="testimonial">
                    <p>"Between the fantasy draft and more games being televised, the usual drought between NCAA seasons has been much less painful. I'm excited to be able to stay engaged with volleyball."</p>
                </div>
                <div class="testimonial">
                    <p>"I really appreciate how interactive this experience has been, especially how it adds a greater fan experience to people who watch, or are trying to learn more about pro volleyball."</p>
                </div>
                <div class="testimonial">
                    <p>"This app is gorgeous. Thanks for putting it out there. And so fun!"</p>
                </div>
                <div class="testimonial">
                    <p>"Y'all are starting something huge that could be a massive growth factor for U.S. volleyball."</p>
                </div>
                <div class="testimonial">
                    <p>"Thank you for your work and for investing in the growth of the sport. Great app and can't wait to continue to support you guys."</p>
                </div>
                <div class="testimonial">
                    <p>"This app is pretty much as user friendly as it gets. I was trying to find a way to make this happen just so I could participate, so I was so excited when I saw y'all are on it!"</p>
                </div>
                <div class="testimonial">
                    <p>"So impressed with this app and all of your work."</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

    </main>

